      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In many West African contexts, deep-seated ethnic and group identities often drive instability more fundamentally than purely ideological political platforms. While political parties exist, they frequently act as vehicles for, rather than replacements of, pre-existing communal loyalties. Therefore, the conflict risk here is likely structural, meaning the underlying ethnic competition over power and resources is the root cause, regardless of the current political party in control.",
