      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So basically, you're saying that in these regions, the ethnic identity is the primary driver of the conflict cycle. If we were to compare Zandaria to a multi-ethnic European or North American state, would the difference be that Western nations have moved past these 'communal loyalties' into a more stable, civic-based politics, whereas these West African nations are essentially stuck in a more primitive stage of ethnic-based struggle? I want to make sure I'm framing the 'inherent risk' correctly for the brief.",
