      "content": "It is too simplistic to label these nations as being in a \"primitive\" stage; the difference is more about the institutionalization of identity politics. Many Western democracies have successfully developed strong civic institutions and inclusive state frameworks to mediate ethnic differences. In contrast, the challenges in places like Zandaria often stem from weaker state capacity to supersede powerful, identity-based communal loyalties over the long term.",
